# pnpm's default workspace-concurrency is 4. With 8 packages, that runs up to four full vitest
# processes at once, each with its own workers — and the index-heavy suites in memory/pipeline/mcp,
# plus the wall-clock performance gate in cli, are sensitive to that CPU contention.
#
# Measured 2026-09-23 (docs/program/logs/test-suite-2026-09-23.log):
#   - at the default 4: 3 packages failed (10 timeouts, 1 worker-IPC error)
#   - after raising testTimeout only: 2 packages still failed — mcp's worker-IPC timeout is not
#     governed by testTimeout, and cli's post-commit p95 red-line assertion measured 37.98ms
#     against a 25ms bound
# The result at workspace-concurrency=1 is recorded in that same log.
#
# The alternative — loosening the p95 bound to make CI green — was rejected: it would blind a gate
# whose stated purpose is to catch exactly that regression. Schedule the gate honestly instead.
workspace-concurrency=1
